<%# Shared visual spectator cluster for multiplayer game rooms (Durak,
    Battleship, Pong, Connect Four) - a pile of little "viewer" icons in the
    page's unused left-hand margin on wide screens, standing in for the
    numeric "N watching" text those pages already show elsewhere. Hidden below
    xl (no room there) via the class below, and hidden entirely at 0 viewers
    via inline style (see spectatorCluster.js) - inline style wins the
    cascade either way, so JS can force it off even on a wide viewport.
    Wired by public/js/games/spectatorCluster.js's window.initSpectatorCluster()
    through these fixed ids - a game view just includes this partial and its
    client calls that once, then feeds it a live spectator count. %>
<div id="spectator-cluster"
     class="hidden xl:flex fixed left-6 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 z-30 flex-col items-center gap-1.5 pointer-events-none">
  <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500"><%= t('games.spectatorsLabel') %></p>
  <div id="spectator-cluster-pile" class="relative w-40 h-40"></div>
</div>
